      "artist": "U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service Headquarters",
      "description": "As a member of the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service Honor Guard, National Wildlife Refuge System Law Enforcement Officer Shelby Finney helped dedicate a Pennsylvania memorial to passengers of Flight 93, killed by terrorists on September 11. Finney, based at Salt Plains National Wildlife Refuge in Oklahoma, was named 2011 Officer of the Year for the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service’s Southwest Region. (USFWS)",
